    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40">

                <pb facs="0123" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg57"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.512/46: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-07-29T14:00:00-04:00">July 29, 1933—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. Your telegram 86, July 28,<anchor n="34" xml:id="d40-f1"/> and despatch No.
                    1487, June 21. Follow General Instruction October 24, 1925, particularly fifth
                        paragraph.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d40-f2"/>
                    <pb facs="0124" n="58" xml:id="pg58"/> With reference to last paragraph of your
                    despatch, limit your protest to payment of tax on fixed charges. Amount of
                    rental contracted before tax law adopted may be treated as fixed charge.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d40-f1" n="34" xml:id="d40-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d40-f2" n="36" xml:id="d40-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed. See note to the German Chargé, July 16, 1926, <ref
                        target="frus1926v01#pg_548"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1926, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 548</ref>; the fifth
                    paragraph mentioned above is identical with the penultimate paragraph, <ref
                        target="frus1926v01#pg_550"><hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p.
                    550</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
